puṉal","gloss":"water-like"}],"gloss":"water-like"},{"surface":"குருதி","parts":[{"text":"குருதி","lemma":"kuruti","gloss":"blood"}],"gloss":"blood"},{"surface":"உலைக்","parts":[{"text":"உலைக்","lemma":"ulai","gloss":"cooking pot"}],"gloss":"in the cooking pot"},{"surface":"கொளீஇத்","parts":[{"text":"கொளீஇத்","lemma":"koḷ","gloss":"having poured"}],"gloss":"having poured"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தொடித்தோள்","parts":[{"text":"தொடித்தோள்","lemma":"toṭittōḷ","gloss":"shoulders with armlets"}],"gloss":"shoulders with armlets"},{"surface":"துடுப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"துடுப்பின்","lemma":"tuṭuppu","gloss":"with ladle"}],"gloss":"with ladle"},{"surface":"துழந்த","parts":[{"text":"துழந்த","lemma":"tuḻavu","gloss":"stirred"}],"gloss":"stirred"},{"surface":"வல்சியின்","parts":[{"text":"வல்சியின்","lemma":"valci","gloss":"like food"}],"gloss":"like food"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அடுகளம்","parts":[{"text":"அடுகளம்","lemma":"aṭukaḷam","gloss":"battlefield of sacrifice"}],"gloss":"battlefield of sacrifice"},{"surface":"வேட்ட","parts":[{"text":"வேட்ட","lemma":"vēḷ","gloss":"sacrificed"}],"gloss":"sacrificed"},{"surface":"அடுபோர்ச்","parts":[{"text":"அடுபோர்ச்","lemma":"aṭupōr","gloss":"deadly warring"}],"gloss":"deadly warring"},{"surface":"செழிய","parts":[{"text":"செழிய","lemma":"ceḻiyaṉ","gloss":"O Ceḻiyaṉ"}],"gloss":"O Ceḻiyaṉ!"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆன்ற","parts":[{"text":"ஆன்ற","lemma":"āl","gloss":"abundant"}],"gloss":"abundant"},{"surface":"கேள்வி","parts":[{"text":"கேள்வி","lemma":"kēḷvi","gloss":"learning"}],"gloss":"scriptural learning"},{"surface":"அடங்கிய","parts":[{"text":"அடங்கிய","lemma":"aṭaṅku","gloss":"disciplined"}],"gloss":"disciplined"},{"surface":"கொள்கை","parts":[{"text":"கொள்கை","lemma":"koḷkai","gloss":"principles"}],"gloss":"principles"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நான்மறை","parts":[{"text":"நான்மறை","lemma":"nāṉmaṟai","gloss":"four Vedas"}],"gloss":"four Vedas"},{"surface":"முதல்வர்","parts":[{"text":"முதல்வர்","lemma":"mutalvar","gloss":"priests"}],"gloss":"priests"},{"surface":"சுற்ற","parts":[{"text":"சுற்ற","lemma":"cuṟṟam","gloss":"retinue"}],"gloss":"retinue"},{"surface":"மாக","parts":[{"text":"மாக","lemma":"āka","gloss":"to be"}],"gloss":"as"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மன்னர்","parts":[{"text":"மன்னர்","lemma":"maṉṉar","gloss":"kings"}],"gloss":"kings"},{"surface":"ஏவல்","parts":[{"text":"ஏவல்","lemma":"ēval","gloss":"bidding"}],"gloss":"bidding"},{"surface":"செய்ய","parts":[{"text":"செய்ய","lemma":"cey","gloss":"to do"}],"gloss":"to do"},{"surface":"மன்னிய","parts":[{"text":"மன்னிய","lemma":"maṉṉu","gloss":"enduring"}],"gloss":"enduring"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேள்வி","parts":[{"text":"வேள்வி","lemma":"vēḷvi","gloss":"sacrifices"}],"gloss":"sacrifices"},{"surface":"முற்றிய","parts":[{"text":"முற்றிய","lemma":"muṟṟu","gloss":"completed"}],"gloss":"completed"},{"surface":"வாய்வாள்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்வாள்","lemma":"vāyvāḷ","gloss":"sharp-sworded"}],"gloss":"sharp-sworded"},{"surface":"வேந்தே","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தே","lemma":"vēntu","gloss":"O King"}],"gloss":"O King!"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நோற்றோர்","parts":[{"text":"நோற்றோர்","lemma":"nōl","gloss":"those who performed penance"}],"gloss":"those who performed penance"},{"surface":"மன்ற","parts":[{"text":"மன்ற","lemma":"maṉṟa","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"பகைவர்","parts":[{"text":"பகைவர்","lemma":"pakaivar","gloss":"enemies"}],"gloss":"enemies"},{"surface":"நின்னொடு","parts":[{"text":"நின்னொடு","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"with you"}],"gloss":"with you"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மாற்றார்","parts":[{"text":"மாற்றார்","lemma":"māṟṟār","gloss":"foes"}],"gloss":"foes"},{"surface":"என்னும்","parts":[{"text":"என்னும்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"called"}],"gloss":"called"},{"surface":"பெயர்","parts":[{"text":"பெயர்","lemma":"peyar","gloss":"name"}],"gloss":"the name"},{"surface":"பெற்று","parts":[{"text":"பெற்று","lemma":"peṟu","gloss":"having obtained"}],"gloss":"having obtained"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆற்றார்","parts":[{"text":"ஆற்றார்","lemma":"māṟṟār","gloss":"unable"}],"gloss":"unable to resist"},{"surface":"ஆயினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயினும்","lemma":"āyiṉum","gloss":"even though"}],"gloss":"even though"},{"surface":"ஆண்டுவாழ்","parts":[{"text":"ஆண்டுவாழ்","lemma":"āṇṭuvāḻ","gloss":"living there"}],"gloss":"living there"},{"surface":"வோரே","parts":[{"text":"வோரே","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"they"}],"gloss":"they"}]}],"literal":"In the deep, dark abyss of the vast ocean / like a ship battered by the wind / elephants went and cleared the field / in that wide place cleared of the field / bearing spears with shining blades / having churned the battle so that kings fell / having seized their war drums so that their fame spread / with crowned heads as the cooking hearth / pouring water-like blood into the cooking pot / with shoulders wearing armlets as the ladle, stirring the food / O Ceḻiyaṉ of deadly war who desired the sacrifice of the battlefield! / With the disciplined principles of abundant scriptural learning / having the priests of the four Vedas as your retinue / while other kings do your bidding, O enduring / king of the sharp sword who completed the sacrifices! / Indeed, those who performed penance are your enemies, who with you / obtained the name of adversaries / even though they were unable to resist, they are those who live there!","translation":"Like a ship tossed and battered by fierce winds in the deep, dark waters of the vast ocean, your war elephants charged and cleared the battlefield. In that wide arena, bearing spears with shining blades, you churned the battle till rival kings fell, and seized their war drums to spread your fame. You performed the sacrifice of the battlefield: using crowned heads of slain kings as hearthstones, pouring their water-like blood into the cooking pot, and stirring this gruesome feast with the strong, armlet-wearing shoulders of the dead as ladles, O Ceḻiyaṉ of deadly war! Guided by the disciplined principles of abundant Vedic learning, surrounded by the priests of the four Vedas as your council, you completed great sacrifices while other kings stood waiting to do your bidding, O enduring king of the sharp sword! Indeed, your enemies must have performed great penance in their past lives; for by earning the title of your adversaries, even though they could not withstand your might, they now dwell eternally in the heavens!","modern":"பரந்த கடலின் ஆழமான இருண்ட பகுதியில் காற்று மோதிய கலம் போல, உனது யானைகள் போர்க்களத்திற்குச் சென்று பகைவர்களை அழித்து இடத்தை அகலப்படுத்தின. அவ்வாறு அகலப்படுத்தப்பட்ட பரந்த போர்க்களத்தில், ஒளிரும் இலை வடிவ வேல்களை ஏந்தி, பகை அரசர்கள் மடியுமாறு போரிட்டு, அவர்களின் புகழை அழித்து முரசுகளைக் கவர்ந்தாய். வெட்டப்பட்ட பகைவர்களின் முடிகொண்ட தலைகளை அடுப்பாகக் கொண்டு, அவர்களின் பெருகியோடும் குருதியை உலையாகக் கூட்டி, வீரவளையல் அணிந்த தோள்களைத் துடுப்பாகக் கொண்டு துழாவிய போர்க்களப் பலியை விரும்பிச் செய்த கொடிய போர் புரியும் செழியனே! சிறந்த வேதக் கல்வியும் அடக்கமும் கொண்ட நான்மறை அந்தணர்களை உனது சுற்றமாகக் கொண்டு, ஏனைய மன்னர்கள் உனது ஏவலுக்குக் காத்திருக்க, நிலைபெற்ற வேள்விகளைச் செய்து முடித்த கூர்மையான வாளையுடைய வேந்தனே! உன்னோடு பகைமை கொண்டு உனது மாற்றார் என்னும் பெயரைப் பெற்ற உனது பகைவர்கள், உன்னை எதிர்க்கும் ஆற்றல் இல்லாதவர் ஆயினும், அவர்கள் உண்மையில் தவம் செய்தவர்கள் ஆவர்; ஏனெனில் அவர்கள் உன்னால் மடிந்து இப்போது வீரசுவர்க்கத்தில் வாழ்கின்றார்கள்!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai (victory) and the Arasa vākai tuṟai, celebrating the military and ritual triumphs of the Pāṇṭiya king Talaiyālaṅkāṉattuc Ceruveṉṟa Neṭuñceḻiyaṉ. The poet, Māṅkuṭi Kiḻavar, praises the king's terrifying victory on the battlefield through the metaphor of a gruesome sacrifice (kaḷavēḷvi), where the heads of slain kings serve as hearthstones and their blood as the boiling broth. He contrasts this martial violence with the king's piety and devotion to Vedic rituals, performed under the guidance of learned priests. The climax of the poem offers a brilliant compliment: the king's defeated enemies are declared to be highly fortunate and virtuous. Though they lacked the strength to defeat him, simply by being named his adversaries and dying by his hand, they attained the ultimate reward of dwelling in the warrior's heaven.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}